ramp_simulation
A simplified Ramp spend-sync: a cleared card swipe becomes a webhook, gets coded
to a GL account, and posts a journal entry in a mock ERP.
The story
Dwight Schrute (Dunder Mifflin, Scranton) charges fake fire drill expenses
on a Ramp card at Schrute Safety Supply. Ramp emits transactions.cleared.
This project:
Extracts the base webhook payload (event id + transaction id)
Fetches the full transaction (Ramp's API response)
Maps it onto GL 6100 Office Expenses — a valid expense account
Returns the ERP journal (debit Office Expenses, credit Ramp Card Liability)
Run it
python3 main.py
​
No extra packages required. Python 3.10+ is enough.
